    "basis": "Sample the source elevation on the former principal courtyard route near Fort Street. The 1860 forecourt and individual footing elevations are inferred separately."
  },
  "notes": "The historical east gate follows Fort Street on Government Street, and the west gate follows the same line toward Wharf Street. City survey and commemorative brickwork tie the northern palisade and northeast bastion to Government and Bastion Square. The southwest bastion is inside the present Broughton and Wharf corner. Fawcett’s eyewitness text and the Maritime Museum tour support reconstruction of a nearly rectangular enclosure inside the four modern streets. The width is an estimate from the street and marker alignment, with the north–south extent close to the roughly 465 feet described after the 1847 enlargement.",
